# The effect of a pointer with no wrap bit: full and empty cannot be told apart, so full never asserts.
id: M04
desc: full never asserts (as with pointers that lack the wrap bit)
intended: a_full_def
edit: rtl/sync_fifo.sv
  find: assign full  = (wr_ptr[AW-1:0] == rd_ptr[AW-1:0]) && (wr_ptr[AW] != rd_ptr[AW]);
  replace: assign full  = 1'b0;
